  "text": "The drawbacks next: salt stacks up quickly. The USDA record contains 907 milligrams of sodium per 100 grams, which is a real tradeoff hidden outside the visible mineral rows. Acidity can bother reflux. Tomato and vinegar make this a rough fit for some people whose reflux is triggered by acidic foods. Squeeze bottles encourage portion creep. A freehand squirt is easy to underestimate, especially when the sauce is spread across chips, burgers, or several parts of a meal.",
